---

### Q&As by page (for voice-check)

**clarity**
1. "What does the Clarity Audit day cover?" → One full day on site following six areas, written report within five working days.
2. "How does the 3x guarantee work?" → If the report does not identify at least three times the fee in recoverable cost or lost revenue, it is refunded in full.
3. "What happens after the Clarity Audit?" → Written report, debrief walked through in person, then yours to act on with or without.

**retained**
1. "What does a fractional CTO do?" → Ongoing technology leadership without the cost of a full-time hire. Scope and cadence agreed at the start.
2. "What are the three tiers?" → Advisory, Embedded, Programme. Six-month minimum on all three.
3. "When does a fractional CTO relationship not work?" → When a business has not worked out what is actually broken yet.

**transform**
1. "What is Transform?" → The programme that follows a Clarity Audit when proper change is needed. ERP, eCommerce and process redesign, run as one programme over weeks.
2. "Does Transform include buying software?" → Every vendor quotes against the same brief, no commission, whichever platform you choose.
3. "How is Transform priced?" → Scoped per engagement, no published price. Starts with a full day on site and a written plan.

**how-i-build**
1. "What are the three rungs?" → Buy off the shelf, buy plus a custom layer (the normal answer), full custom (last resort).
2. "Does Decoded Ops resell software?" → No. No vendor pays for a recommendation. Own software scored the same way.
3. "Will I see the cost of options that were not recommended?" → Yes. Every option priced, including the ones not recommended.

**data-app**
1. "What does the Data App actually do?" → Supplier feeds, data enrichment, catalogue maintenance, orders, purchasing, stock, production and despatch.
2. "Does it replace my existing platform?" → Can run alongside or replace it. Feeds land, get matched and enriched, pushed back clean.
3. "How are supplier feeds handled?" → Land in the Data App, matched, enriched, pushed back. No re-keying.

**artwork-manager**
1. "What does the Artwork Manager do?" → Artwork vault across embroidery and print formats, versioned with audit trail. Customers approve their own proofs.
2. "How does customer proofing work?" → Customers get their own accounts, approve proofs against the version actually shown. Recorded against that version.
3. "What are founding-client terms?" → Full implementation pricing, first six months support waived, named reference.

**commerce**
1. "What are the three tiers?" → Core, Standard (B2B trade portal shape), Extended (multi-site, ERP integration, bespoke).
2. "How is this different from a bespoke build?" → Built on Medusa B2B open-source core. Comes in well under the 8,000-20,000 pound bespoke range.
3. "Does it integrate with ERP systems like Khaos Control?" → ERP integration is Extended tier. Full migration scoped separately.

**awards-engraving**
1. "How do you manage variable data for awards?" → Audit how data comes in and gets checked, find systems built for variable-data personalisation.
2. "How does production schedule around event deadlines?" → Production schedules backwards from the date, most systems do not.
3. "What about proof approval when there are 50 personalised items?" → Maps the workflow and finds the bottlenecks.

**labels-packaging**
1. "What makes labels and packaging different from other print?" → Print, compliance, supply chain meet. No tolerance for error, turnaround always tight.
2. "Can you help with EDI integration for bigger customers?" → Assessed as part of the audit.
3. "How do you handle variable data at speed?" → Reviews workflow from file intake to press-ready output, recommends systems built for it.

**promotional-merchandise**
1. "How do you manage multiple supplier ranges?" → Audit maps full workflow from client enquiry to delivery.
2. "How does the artwork approval loop work?" → Customers approve their own proofs, version-controlled, no email chain.
3. "How do I know where margin is leaking?" → Audit puts a number on every finding in time, margin, and admin cost.

**schoolwear**
1. "How do you handle the back-to-school peak?" → Find where supplier data lag creates orders you cannot fulfil before peak season.
2. "How does badge and embroidery management work at scale?" → Dedicated workflow that spreadsheets were never built for.
3. "Does the Decoded Data App replace my existing platform?" → Can run alongside or as the full system.

**signs-graphics**
1. "How does the workflow differ from generic ERP?" → Job starts with a site survey, not an order. Most systems cannot track survey through to sign-off.
2. "How do you cost jobs with so much variation?" → Reviews how you cost jobs and where margin goes.
3. "Can you help with installation scheduling?" → Looks at how installation scheduling connects to production.

**teamwear-clubwear**
1. "How do you handle squad-level personalisation data?" → Finds where personalisation data is managed by hand.
2. "How does production schedule around seasonal deadlines?" → Works backwards from the first match date.
3. "How do you fix the proof and approval bottleneck?" → Fixing that loop wins back more time than anywhere else in the job.

**workwear**
1. "How do you fix supplier feed chaos?" → Maps where re-keying happens.
2. "How do you get decoration and stock in the same picture?" → Systems that do not understand plain vs decorated SKU force workarounds.
3. "How do you manage blank stock dependency?" → Checks blank stock against committed orders for supply gaps.
